    "description": "0-Vita-1 is a Vithia protocol for separating deterministic context compilation from downstream decision-making while preserving typed provenance, immutable predecessor states, explicit uncertainty, and append-only custody. The v0.1.0 evidence package reports simulated experiments E0-E3 and a frozen E4A Space Invaders snapshot input set. The package distinguishes identity from meaning, custody from correctness, prediction from observation, and declared FCG relationships from causality. Negative, null, partial, deferred, and not-computed states are preserved.",
